  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "1. Weights W and activations X sit in HBM3e (192 GB, 7.37 TB/s).",
      "focus": [
        "hbm-dram-left",
        "hbm-dram-right",
        "hbm-base-left",
        "hbm-base-right"
      ],
      "dot": "hbm-dram-left",
      "explode": 0.6,
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "hbm"
    },
    {
      "text": "2. If a tile lives on a neighboring chip in the pod, it crosses an ICI link (1.2 TB/s bidirectional) wired directly into the 3D torus — no switch hop needed.",
      "focus": [
        "ici-link"
      ],
      "dot": "ici-link",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "ici"
    },
    {
      "text": "3. Data lands in VMEM, the TensorCore's 64 MiB on-chip scratchpad.",
      "focus": [
        "tensor-core-a"
      ],
      "dot": "tensor-core-a",
      "drill": "tensor-core-detail",
      "stage": "shared-memory"
    },
    {
      "text": "4. Weights are loaded into an MXU's 256×256 systolic array and stay resident there for the whole matmul — this is the TPU's 'weight-stationary' design.",
      "focus": [
        "mxu"
      ],
      "dot": "mxu",
      "drill": "tensor-core-detail",
      "stage": "tensor-core"
    },
    {
      "text": "5. Zooming into the array (shown as a representative 8×8 grid): each PE cell now holds one stationary weight in its local register.",
      "focus": [
        "pe-cell"
      ],
      "dot": "pe-cell",
      "drill": "mxu-grid",
      "stage": "weight-load"
    },
    {
      "text": "6. Activations enter from the left edge and advance one column per cycle. Each PE multiplies its stationary weight by the activation passing through.",
      "focus": [
        "activation-edge",
        "pe-cell"
      ],
      "dot": "activation-edge",
      "drill": "mxu-grid",
      "stage": "wavefront"
    },
    {
      "text": "7. Partial sums flow downward from PE to PE in lockstep with the activations, so the whole array works as one diagonal wavefront — no register file or warp scheduler involved, unlike a GPU's Tensor Core.",
      "focus": [
        "pe-cell"
      ],
      "dot": "pe-cell",
      "drill": "mxu-grid",
      "stage": "systolic-flow"
    },
    {
      "text": "8. Finished partial sums drain out of the bottom row of the array.",
      "focus": [
        "psum-edge"
      ],
      "dot": "psum-edge",
      "drill": "mxu-grid",
      "stage": "accumulate"
    },
    {
      "text": "9. The Vector Unit runs the epilogue on the MXU's output: bias add, activation function, normalization.",
      "focus": [
        "vector-unit"
      ],
      "dot": "vector-unit",
      "drill": "tensor-core-detail",
      "stage": "epilogue"
    },
    {
      "text": "10. The Scalar Unit advances loop counters and addressing for the next tile; SparseCores concurrently handle any embedding-table gather/scatter against HBM.",
      "focus": [
        "scalar-unit"
      ],
      "dot": "scalar-unit",
      "drill": "tensor-core-detail",
      "stage": "scalar"
    },
    {
      "text": "11. Results move from VMEM back to HBM3e; with model/data parallelism, ICI links all-reduce partial results with other chips in the pod.",
      "focus": [
        "ici-link",
        "hbm-dram-left"
      ],
      "dot": "ici-link",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "writeback"
    }
  ],
